keywords:
  - "post-quantum cryptography"
  - "information-theoretic security"
  - "device-independent QKD"
  - "ML-KEM-768"
  - "SLH-DSA"
  - "Carter-Wegman MAC"
  - "Shamir secret sharing"
  - "quantum geometric tensor"
  - "bivariate-bicycle qLDPC"
  - "Lean 4 formal verification"
abstract: >-
  Clean-room cryptographic refactoring of legacy SecMesh (aff7dc6) rebuilt atop
  Tsotchke's MIT/Apache-2.0 stack (moonlab, QGTL, libirrep, spin_based_neural_network,
  Eshkol, Rosette-Wire, pq-consensus-bandwidth) into a Post-Quantum and
  Post-Super-Intelligence (information-theoretic) defense suite, backed by 27
  zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0 theorems verified across all six distinct proof kernels
  via lake comparator --paranoid and two companion AMS-LaTeX white papers.
